1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,837
Hey everyone!

2
00:00:01,787 --> 00:00:05,387
Quick update on MEMENTO for Hack Club's Half Life.

3
00:00:05,387 --> 00:00:11,162
I just wrapped up the first 5 hours of planning and architecture, and here is how it is shaping up.

4
00:00:11,162 --> 00:00:16,325
Most voice recorders dump gigabytes of audio into a folder you never listen to.

5
00:00:16,325 --> 00:00:22,437
MEMENTO is a wearable hardware recorder that turns conversations into structured personal memory.

6
00:00:22,437 --> 00:00:33,575
At its core is an ESP32-S3 and an INMP441 I2S digital MEMS microphone recording uncompressed 16-bit audio straight to a 32GB microSD card.

7
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:41,125
For privacy, I designed in a physical hardware slide switch that cuts power directly to the microphone so it cannot record in secret.

8
00:00:41,125 --> 00:00:49,275
It syncs with your Mac over USB-C where local AI handles transcription, speaker separation, and interview coaching with zero cloud tracking.

9
00:00:49,275 --> 00:00:54,850
Next up: routing the 2-layer PCB in KiCad and modeling the clip-on enclosure.

10
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:56,750
Thanks for watching!

